    "notes": "TIRF imaging of bacteriophage T7 replisomes (gp4 helicase, LD655-gp5/trx polymerase, gp2.5 SSB) on surface-tethered ~27 kb forked DNA, with linear and new transverse DNA flow-stretching configurations resolving parental, leading and lagging strands and replisome rotation; topologically unconstrained (single biotin) vs constrained (multi-biotin handle) substrates. Forces on DNA arches and the replisome are estimated from extensions with a WLC model (A = 50 nm, T = 296.15 K) rather than measured directly."
